  "label": "Watermelon and Fried Chicken Food Stereotype",
  "description": "A historical and racist stereotype that portrays Black people as being inherently associated with eating watermelon and fried chicken, reducing them to caricatures of their eating habits and dehumanizing them. This stereotype is used in the meme to mock the Black woman's food preference, implying she is irrational or overly picky, which reinforces racial bias and discrimination.",
